{
  "configuration_id": "config_023",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_036 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile) is the current best at 0.706 acc, and scvi_n200 is clearly the dominant RNA encoder (0.706 vs 0.635 for pca_n2000 vs 0.542 for scgpt). However, every experiment to date has used imagenet_vit_l as the image encoder, leaving the image-encoder dimension completely unexplored. Question: config_023 changes only the image encoder (imagenet_vit_l → resnet50) while holding all other settings at their known-best values (scvi_n200, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile), cleanly isolating whether the choice of image encoder matters when paired with the best RNA encoder. Why this is the best next experiment: (1) it addresses a major source of uncertainty—zero data on resnet50 in any multimodal setting; (2) it is a single-variable change from the current best, making the result directly interpretable; (3) if resnet50 is competitive, it broadens the design space and may reveal that the image encoder is less critical than the RNA encoder; if it is substantially worse, it confirms imagenet_vit_l as the right choice and lets us focus remaining budget on aggregation/fusion refinements around config_036."
}

